== live Gamma rule text: Sep-30 market ==

--- which-cities-face-tornado-risk-on-september-30-2026 / which-cities-face-tornado-risk-on-september-30-2026-chicago-il ---
resolutionSource=https://www.spc.noaa.gov/products/outlook/day1otlk.html
feeSchedule={"exponent": 1, "rate": 0.05, "rebateRate": 0.25, "takerOnly": true}
RULE: If the city's coordinates fall inside any area rated 2% or higher, that city resolves "Yes".
RULE: Each city's coordinates and the polygon boundaries are publicly verifiable.
RULE: Borderline cases can be independently confirmed using the polygon data (excluding the hatched SIGN overlay, which is not a probability rating) and the city's listed coordinates.
RULE: The point-in-polygon test is performed on unprojected WGS84 (EPSG:4326) coordinates, which is the native coordinate system of the SPC GeoJSON data.
RULE: Resolution is based on the scheduled 01:00 UTC Day 1 Convective Outlook update issued on the following UTC calendar day.
RULE: That scheduled update is the revisions cutoff; subsequent revisions published after it will not be considered.
RULE: If the SPC Day 1 Convective Outlook has not been published by the time the market closes, this market will resolve to "No".
RULE: In the case that the Resolution Source publishes data, sufficient to settle a Market, that is clearly erroneous and the result of technical or operational error, or of unauthorized interference with the Resolution Source or its data, the Market may remain open for a period of up to seven (7) calendar days (ET) from the time of the original release, in anticipation of a correction by the Resolution Source.
RULE: If the Resolution Source publishes a corrected value within that period, that value will be eligible for resolution.
RULE: The resolution source for this market is the NOAA Storm Prediction Center at spc.noaa.gov.
RULE: This market uses coordinates 41.8781, -87.6298 for Chicago, IL.

